{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Enumerative.Partition","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Sign","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.End","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MonoidAlgebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossKappa","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter"],"declarations":44,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.card_irreducibles_eq_card_partitions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.card_irreducibles_eq_card_partitions","kind":"theorem","line":890,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L890-L906","doc":"**The count corollary (the punchline).**  The number of iso-classes of\nirreducible `k[S_n]`-modules equals the number of partitions of `n`.\n\nWe phrase the left-hand side as `Fintype.card (PartitionIndex n)` — the number of\n*Specht* modules — which equals the number of irreducibles by\n`specht_pairwise_noniso` (they are distinct) + `specht_exhausts_irreducibles`\n(they are all of them).  The right-hand side `Fintype.card (Nat.Partition n)` is\nthe partition count.  This is the identity that pins the Wedderburn block count of\n`k[S_n]` to `#{λ ⊢ n}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.specht_exhausts_irreducibles","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.specht_exhausts_irreducibles","kind":"theorem","line":737,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L737-L888","doc":"**Completeness.**  Every simple `k[S_n]`-module is isomorphic to some Specht\nmodule.  Phrased: for any representation `ρ : Representation k (Perm (Fin n)) W`\nthat is simple as a `k[S_n]`-module — stated as\n`IsSimpleModule (MonoidAlgebra k (Perm (Fin n))) ρ.asModule`, using the\n`MonoidAlgebra k G`-module structure on `ρ.asModule` (Mathlib\n`Representation.asModule`) — there is a Young diagram `μ` with `nOf μ = n` and a\nrepresentation isomorphism `ρ ≅ spechtRep μ` (after transporting the acting group\nalong `nOf μ = n`).\n\nThis is the half of the classification that says the Specht modules **exhaust** the\nirreducibles.\n\n## Proved\n\nThe Specht modules are `#partitions` many pairwise non-isomorphic simples\n(`specht_isSimple` + `specht_pairwise_noniso`), and there are no others. The\n\"no others\" half is a **count**, every step of it a bound:\n\n    #{pairwise non-isomorphic simples}\n      ≤ dim_k {class functions on Sₙ}      characters are independent class functions\n      ≤ #conj classes of Sₙ                a class function is its values on classes\n      ≤ #partitions of n                   cycle type separates conjugacy classes\n\nAssuming an extra simple `W` isomorphic to no `S^μ` gives `#partitions + 1`\npairwise non-isomorphic simples, contradicting the chain.\n\nIndependence of the characters comes from the pairing\n\n    ⅟|G| • Σ_g χ_V(g⁻¹)·χ_W(g) = dim_k Hom_G(V, W)\n\n(`RepresentationCharacter.charPairing_eq_finrank_homG`), which is **diagonal**\nby Schur and has **nonzero diagonal** because the identity is equivariant. Note\nwhat is *not* needed: `FDRep.char_orthonormal` normalises that diagonal to `1`\nand carries `[IsAlgClosed k]` to do it, but a bound only needs the diagonal\nnonzero — so the whole argument runs over an arbitrary characteristic-zero\nfield, `ℚ` included.\n\n`#print axioms` reports `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`.\n\n## Supporting modules\n\n| Module | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter` | character theory on `Representation`, off Mathlib's `FDRep` category layer; Schur; the count |\n| `QOU.MathlibExt.GroupAlgebraCenter` | class functions and their dimension; conjugacy classes inject into partitions |\n| `QOU.MathlibExt.GramNondegenerate` | a diagonal Gram matrix with nonzero diagonal gives linear independence |\n\nCloses bean sp06. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtRepAt_noniso","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtRepAt_noniso","kind":"theorem","line":720,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L720-L735","doc":"Distinct shapes stay non-isomorphic after the transport. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtRepAt_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtRepAt_stable","kind":"theorem","line":712,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L712-L718","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtRepAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtRepAt","kind":"def","line":706,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L706-L710","doc":"`S^μ` as a representation of `Perm (Fin n)`, for `h : nOf μ = n`.  This is\nthe composite that `specht_exhausts_irreducibles` compares against. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.transportPermHom_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.transportPermHom_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":702,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L702-L704","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtRep_stable_eq_bot_or_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtRep_stable_eq_bot_or_top","kind":"theorem","line":672,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L672-L692","doc":"`specht_isSimple`, transported from submodules of `M^μ` inside `S^μ` to\nsubmodules of the carrier `S^μ` itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtSubmodule_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtSubmodule_nontrivial","kind":"instance","line":666,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L666-L670","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtSubmodule_finite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtSubmodule_finite","kind":"instance","line":660,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L660-L664","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.specht_pairwise_noniso","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.specht_pairwise_noniso","kind":"theorem","line":635,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L635-L651","doc":"**Pairwise non-isomorphism.**  Distinct shapes give non-isomorphic Specht\nmodules: if `μ ≠ ν` (with the same number of cells, so they index the *same*\nsymmetric group), then `S^μ` and `S^ν` are not isomorphic as `S_n`-representations.\n\nWe state it via the intertwiner predicate over the shared carrier index `nOf μ`,\nusing the hypothesis `h : nOf μ = nOf ν` to view `spechtRep ν` as a representation\nof `Perm (Fin (nOf μ))` (by transporting along `h`).\n\n**Now sorry-free modulo the single James core** `spechtIso_imp_dom_both`: an\nisomorphism gives dominance both ways, and the proved `partitionDom_antisymm`\nturns that into `μ = ν`, contradicting `μ ≠ ν`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtIso_imp_dom_both","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtIso_imp_dom_both","kind":"theorem","line":601,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L601-L633","doc":"**James/Sagan cross-shape dominance — PROVED.**  A representation isomorphism\n`S^μ ≅ S^ν` (over the shared group via `h`) forces dominance both ways:\n`partitionDom μ ν ∧ partitionDom ν μ`.\n\nSagan Thm 2.4.4.  Each direction is `dom_of_intertwiner` above; the reverse one\nre-indexes the acting group through `transportPermHom h.symm`, using that the two\ntransports are mutually inverse.\n\nMathlib packages neither the cross-shape dominance bound nor the tableau\ncombinatorics it rests on; the ingredients are built in\n`QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossDominance` (Sagan Lemma 2.2.6) and\n`QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossKappa` (the cross-shape `κ_t`).\n\n`#print axioms` reports `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.dom_of_intertwiner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.dom_of_intertwiner","kind":"theorem","line":569,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L569-L599","doc":"**Sagan Thm 2.4.4 for an isomorphism.**  A `k`-linear intertwiner\n`S^μ ≃ S^ν` (for `Perm (Fin (nOf μ))` acting on `S^ν` through `h`) forces `μ ⊵ ν`.\nImmediate from `dom_of_nonzero_hom` applied to `e` followed by the inclusion\n`S^ν ↪ M^ν`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.dom_of_nonzero_hom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.dom_of_nonzero_hom","kind":"theorem","line":532,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L532-L566","doc":"**Sagan Thm 2.4.4, hom form.**  A nonzero equivariant `θ : S^μ → M^ν` forces\n`μ ⊵ ν`.  This is the general statement; the isomorphism version below is the\nspecial case `θ = (inclusion) ∘ e`.\n\n`θ ≠ 0` gives a polytabloid it does not kill, because the `e_t` span `S^μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.dom_of_kapCross","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.dom_of_kapCross","kind":"theorem","line":454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L454-L529","doc":"The `κ_t` computation at the heart of Sagan Thm 2.4.4 (the step that avoids\nextending `θ` to `M^μ`): because `κ_t e_t = |C_t| e_t` stays inside `S^μ`,\nequivariance of `θ` on `S^μ` alone gives `κ_t (θ e_t) = |C_t| · θ e_t ≠ 0`.\nExpanding `θ e_t` in the `ν`-tabloid basis then produces a tabloid with\n`κ_t {s} ≠ 0`, and Lemma 2.2.6 converts that into dominance: an equivariant\n`θ : S^μ → M^ν` not killing the polytabloid `e_t` forces `μ ⊵ ν`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.nonempty_tableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.nonempty_tableau","kind":"theorem","line":448,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L448-L451","doc":"Every diagram admits a tableau: `nOf μ` is by definition the number of\ncells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.partitionDom_antisymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.partitionDom_antisymm","kind":"theorem","line":419,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L419-L433","doc":"**Antisymmetry of dominance (sorry-free).** If `μ` dominates `ν` and `ν`\ndominates `μ`, then `μ = ν`: equal partial sums for every `i` force equal\nrow lengths (`Finset.sum_range_succ` + `omega`), and equal row lengths force\nequal cell sets (`YoungDiagram.ext` via `mem_iff_lt_rowLen`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.partitionDom_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.partitionDom_refl","kind":"theorem","line":415,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L415-L416","doc":"Dominance is reflexive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.partitionDom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.partitionDom","kind":"def","line":409,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L409-L413","doc":"**Dominance (majorization) order on Young diagrams**: `μ` dominates `ν`\n(`partitionDom μ ν`) iff every partial row-length sum of `μ` is at least the\ncorresponding partial sum of `ν`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtRepOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtRepOn","kind":"def","line":392,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L392-L397","doc":"`S^ν` viewed as a representation of the *same* group `Perm (Fin (nOf μ))`\nacting on `S^μ`, via `transportPermHom`.  Abbreviation used to state the\nclassification cleanly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.transportPermHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.transportPermHom","kind":"def","line":377,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L377-L390","doc":"**Transport the acting group along a cell-count equality.**  When `h : a = b`,\n`finCongr h : Fin a ≃ Fin b` induces a monoid isomorphism\n`Perm (Fin a) →* Perm (Fin b)` (`Equiv.permCongrHom` as a `MonoidHom`).  Composing a\nrepresentation of `Perm (Fin b)` with this hom yields a representation of\n`Perm (Fin a)`, so two Specht modules of equal-size shapes can be compared by\n`IsRepIso` over **one** group.  This is the precise sense in which \"`S^μ` and `S^ν`\nare both `S_n`-representations\" when `μ` and `ν` have the same number of cells.\n\nKept general in `{a b : ℕ}` (rather than `nOf μ = nOf ν`) so the same transport\nserves both the pairwise-non-iso comparison (`nOf μ = nOf ν`) and the completeness\ncomparison (`nOf μ = n` against a bare `n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.IsRepIso.trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.IsRepIso.trans","kind":"theorem","line":364,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L364-L373","doc":"Representation isomorphism is transitive (compose the intertwining equivs). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.IsRepIso.symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.IsRepIso.symm","kind":"theorem","line":354,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L354-L362","doc":"Representation isomorphism is symmetric (the inverse equiv intertwines). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.IsRepIso.refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.IsRepIso.refl","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L350-L352","doc":"Representation isomorphism is reflexive (the identity equiv intertwines). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.IsRepIso.exists_intertwiner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.IsRepIso.exists_intertwiner","kind":"theorem","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L336-L336","doc":"There exists a `k`-linear equiv intertwining the two actions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.IsRepIso.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.IsRepIso.mk","kind":"ctor","line":332,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L332-L332","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.IsRepIso","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.IsRepIso","kind":"structure","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L323-L337","doc":"**Two representations are isomorphic** when there is a `k`-linear equivalence\nbetween their carriers that **intertwines** the group actions.  This is the honest,\nplumbing-free notion of \"`V ≅ V'` as `G`-representations\": a `k`-linear\nisomorphism `e` with `e (ρ g x) = ρ' g (e x)` for all `g, x`.\n\nFor Specht modules of *different* shapes the carriers `S^μ` and `S^ν` sit in\ndifferent ambient modules, and the *same* abstract group `Perm (Fin n)` acts on\nboth (here `n = μ.card = ν.card`), so this is exactly the statement that compares\nthem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtRep_apply_coe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtRep_apply_coe","kind":"theorem","line":315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L315-L319","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.spechtRep","kind":"def","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L298-L312","doc":"**`S^μ` as a representation of `S_n`.**  The restriction of `Specht.Mtab.rep μ`\nto the stable submodule `S^μ`, packaged as a genuine\n`Representation k (Perm (Fin n)) (S^μ)`.  Each generator acts by\n`LinearMap.restrict` of `Mtab.rep μ σ` to `S^μ` (well-defined by\n`specht_smul_mem`).  This is the object on which `IsRepIso` compares `S^μ` and\n`S^ν`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.specht_smul_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.specht_smul_mem","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L279-L296","doc":"**`S^μ` is `S_n`-stable.**  The Specht submodule is invariant under the\npermutation action `Specht.Mtab.rep`: this is what makes the restricted\nrepresentation `spechtRep` below well-formed.  It holds because `rep σ` permutes\npolytabloids (`e_t ↦ ±e_{σ•t}`), which span `S^μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.rep_polytabloid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.rep_polytabloid","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L245-L276","doc":"**`rep σ` permutes polytabloids: `σ · e_t = e_{σ•t}`.**  The linear action sends\nthe polytabloid of `t` to the polytabloid of `σ • t`, via `map_sum`/`map_zsmul`\n(`rep` is `k`-linear) + `rep_of`, reindexing the column-stabilizer sum along the\nconjugation bijection `conjStabEquiv` (sign is conjugation-invariant in `ℤˣ`, and\n`(σπσ⁻¹) • (σ•t) = σ • (π•t)`).  This is the heart of `S_n`-stability. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.conjStabEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.conjStabEquiv","kind":"def","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L228-L242","doc":"The conjugation bijection `C_t ≃ C_{σ•t}`, `π ↦ σπσ⁻¹`.  It witnesses that the\ncolumn stabilizers of `t` and `σ • t` are conjugate subgroups, the reindexing used\nto push `rep σ` through a polytabloid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.conj_mem_colStab_bwd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.conj_mem_colStab_bwd","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L220-L226","doc":"Conjugation `σ⁻¹ · σ` carries `colStab (σ • t)` back into `colStab t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.conj_mem_colStab_fwd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.conj_mem_colStab_fwd","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L212-L217","doc":"Conjugation `σ · σ⁻¹` carries `colStab t` into `colStab (σ • t)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.card_partitionIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.card_partitionIndex","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L200-L205","doc":"The index set of irreducibles has the same cardinality as the partitions of\n`n` — immediate from the equiv.  (Sorry-free: it is `Fintype.card_congr` of the\nnow-proved `partitionEquivYoungIndex`, no extra content.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.instFintypePartitionIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.instFintypePartitionIndex","kind":"instance","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L193-L198","doc":"There are finitely many Young diagrams of size `n`, **derived** from the\npartition equiv together with `Fintype (Nat.Partition n)` (Mathlib,\n`Mathlib/Combinatorics/Enumerative/Partition.lean`).  This makes the irreducible\ncount below a finite cardinal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.partitionEquivYoungIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.partitionEquivYoungIndex","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L161-L191","doc":"**Partitions of `n` index Young diagrams of size `n`.**  The classical\nbijection `λ ⊢ n ↔ {Young diagram with n cells}` sending a partition to the\ndiagram whose row lengths are its (sorted) parts, with inverse reading off\n`rowLens`.  Built directly from `YoungDiagram.ofRowLens` / `rowLens` and their\nround-trip lemmas — Mathlib has no packaged `YoungDiagram ↔ Nat.Partition`\nbridge at this pin. **Sorry-free.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.ofRowLens_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.ofRowLens_congr","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L156-L159","doc":"`YoungDiagram.ofRowLens` depends only on the underlying list, not the sortedness proof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.sorted_parts_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.sorted_parts_pos","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L151-L154","doc":"The parts of a partition, after sorting, remain positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.card_eq_rowLens_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.card_eq_rowLens_sum","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L146-L149","doc":"`μ.card` equals the sum of its row lengths. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.card_cellsOfRowLens","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.card_cellsOfRowLens","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L129-L144","doc":"The number of cells produced by `cellsOfRowLens w` equals the sum of `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.PartitionIndex.diagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.PartitionIndex.diagram","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L121-L122","doc":"The underlying Young diagram of an index element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.PartitionIndex.instDecidableEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.PartitionIndex.instDecidableEq","kind":"instance","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L118-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.instDecidableEqYoungDiagram_folio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.instDecidableEqYoungDiagram_folio","kind":"instance","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L109-L114","doc":"`YoungDiagram` has decidable equality: a diagram is determined by its `cells`\n`Finset` (the `isLowerSet` field is a `Prop`, irrelevant by proof irrelevance), and\n`Finset (ℕ × ℕ)` has `DecidableEq`.  Mathlib's pinned revision does not `deriving`\nthis, so we supply it via the `cells` injection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.PartitionIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification.PartitionIndex","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtClassification.lean#L103-L107","doc":"The **index type** for the irreducibles of `S_n`: Young diagrams with exactly\n`n` cells.  Carrying it as the subtype `{μ : YoungDiagram // μ.card = n}` gives a\ndirect projection `(·).val : PartitionIndex n → YoungDiagram`, so we can form\n`Specht.SpechtSubmodule` of an index element with no glue. ","signatureChunk":0}]}